<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>GoIteration - Tag - loommii</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/tags/goiteration/</link><description>我的个人技术博客</description><generator>Hugo 0.165.0 &amp; FixIt v0.4.5</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 16 Jan 2026 01:28:43 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://loommii.github.io/en/tags/goiteration/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Go Daily Question 20250609</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_20250609/</link><pubDate>Mon, 09 Jun 2025 11:37:59 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_20250609/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;What is the output value of &lt;code&gt;counter&lt;/code&gt; in the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;package main&#10;&#10;import &amp;#34;fmt&amp;#34;&#10;&#10;func main() {&#10;&#9;var m = map[string]int{&#10;&#9;&#9;&amp;#34;A&amp;#34;: 21,&#10;&#9;&#9;&amp;#34;B&amp;#34;: 22,&#10;&#9;&#9;&amp;#34;C&amp;#34;: 23,&#10;&#9;}&#10;&#9;counter := 0&#10;&#9;for k, v := range m {&#10;&#9;&#9;if counter == 0 {&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;delete(m, &amp;#34;A&amp;#34;)&#10;&#9;&#9;}&#10;&#9;&#9;counter&amp;#43;&amp;#43;&#10;&#9;&#9;fmt.Println(k, v)&#10;&#9;}&#10;&#9;fmt.Println(&amp;#34;counter is &amp;#34;, counter)&#10;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;A. 2&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;B. 3&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;C. 2 or 3&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;C&#10;&lt;a href="https://go.dev/play/p/-OKOFSeE6GS" target="_blank" rel="external nofollow noopener noreferrer"&gt;Go Online Run&lt;/a&gt;&#10;The iteration order of &lt;code&gt;for range map&lt;/code&gt; is unordered. If &lt;code&gt;A&lt;/code&gt; is encountered in the first iteration, the output is 3; otherwise, it is 2.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Go Daily Question 086</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_086/</link><pubDate>Fri, 06 Dec 2024 20:45:12 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_086/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;What is the output of the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;func main() {&#10; m := map[int]string{0:&amp;#34;zero&amp;#34;,1:&amp;#34;one&amp;#34;}&#10; for k,v := range m {&#10; fmt.Println(k,v)&#10; }&#10;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;0 zero&#10;1 one&#10;// Or&#10;1 one&#10;0 zero&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;The output of a map is unordered.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/details&gt;</description></item><item><title>Go Daily Question 001 - Address Traps in range loops</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_001/</link><pubDate>Fri, 06 Dec 2024 19:40:54 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_001/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;In Go programming, the range loop is a common source of pitfalls. This article will delve into a classic problem, exploring the behavior differences before and after Go 1.22.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>